// expect-exit: 0
//
// PROBE 04 — a large `fixed` module-state table.
//
// ASKS: does a module-level `pub fixed` array of ~30 000 small structs compile;
// is it emitted as READ-ONLY DATA rather than filled in by a startup routine;
// is `#size_of` of the row what the cost model assumed; and can a row be
// reached through an index the compiler cannot fold?
//
// DEPENDS ON THE ANSWER: ZONE_MODEL.md Z-7 (the four flat tables), Z-8 (binary
// search over a transition slice), SAFETY.md S-19 (`fixed` module state is
// read-only memory, no initialisation at startup, nothing to leak, nothing to
// race) and TM-007 (the tzdb is compiled in). This is the most expensive
// negative verdict in the set: if a large `fixed` table were initialised at run
// time, TM-007's representation would change before cycle 0.5.
//
// THE EXIT CODE IS ONLY HALF THE VERDICT. It cannot say whether the array is
// static data or filled at startup. The other half is read off the emitted IR
// and the object's sections:
//
//     npkc tests/probe/probe04_big_fixed_table.npk -o p.ll
//     grep 'TRANSITIONS" = constant' p.ll     # must be `constant`, not `global`
//     grep -c llvm.global_ctors p.ll          # must be 0
//     llc ... -o p.o && readelf -SW p.o       # the symbol's section must be .rodata
//
// THAT HALF IS EVIDENCED NEXT DOOR, NOT HERE. Running the four commands above
// against THIS file costs 281 s and 30.9 GiB (O-N4), so it has been done once,
// on 2026-09-03, and `meta/roadmap/0.0/0.0.0.md` §7 records it explicitly as a
// ONE-TIME OBSERVATION that nobody should re-derive casually. The same four
// commands against `probe04b_emission_shape.npk` -- the identical declaration
// at 300 rows -- cost 0.16 s, and their full output is committed verbatim in
// `probe04b_emission_shape.txt`. The emission FORM is chosen by the same
// lowering path at any element count, so 300 rows evidences it; what this file
// keeps for itself is the SIZE claim, that 30 000 rows compile at all and that
// the arithmetic holds at that count.
//
// THE DATA IS SYNTHETIC AND HAS A CLOSED FORM, so this file can be regenerated
// without a generator in `tools/`:
//
//     at_utc[i]     = -2208988800 + i * 604800 + (i % 97) * 3600
//     type_index[i] = i % 13                         for i in 0 .. 29999
//
// The sequence is strictly increasing by construction (the weekly term, 604800,
// exceeds the largest step the hourly term can take back, 96 * 3600), which is
// the invariant Z-8's binary search rests on and which `main` re-proves over
// every row rather than trusting this comment.
mod:probe04_big_fixed_table;

pub struct:ZoneTransition = { int64:at_utc; int32:type_index; };

